    "type": "function",
    "function": {
      "name": "get_map_of_dom",
      "description": "Returns a compact, truncated map of the page DOM structure. The map is optimized for understanding the overall page layout: 1. Single-child wrapper chains are collapsed. Their attributes are merged into a comment indicating count. 2. Repeating sibling elements show only the first with a comment indicating count. 3. Only semantic attributes are kept: class, id, role, aria-label, label, alt, type, and data-* attributes. Can only be called once per session; later calls return the previous result message.",
